#: constants/HelpData.ts:327
msgid "Open Friends from the menu to manage your connections; you need to be signed in and online. On the Search tab, enter a friend's exact email address and send them a friend request. Email addresses are never shown to other users. Incoming and sent requests appear in the Requests tab; tap Accept to confirm or Decline to ignore. A badge on the Friends menu item shows how many pending requests are waiting. Once a request is accepted, both users appear in each other's Friends list and can view each other's shared content. To remove a friend, long-press them in your list. Pull down on the list to refresh it."
msgstr "Open Friends from the menu to manage your connections; you need to be signed in and online. On the Search tab, enter a friend's exact email address and send them a friend request. Email addresses are never shown to other users. Incoming and sent requests appear in the Requests tab; tap Accept to confirm or Decline to ignore. A badge on the Friends menu item shows how many pending requests are waiting. Once a request is accepted, both users appear in each other's Friends list and can view each other's shared content. To remove a friend, long-press them in your list. Pull down on the list to refresh it."

#: app/(app)/settings.tsx:432
msgid "Open Settings"
msgstr "Open Settings"

#: constants/HelpData.ts:223
msgid "Open the Exercise Library from the menu at any time to browse almost 1,000 exercises, and filter by body part, target muscle, or equipment. Search understands common abbreviations like RDL, OHP, DB, and KB, and forgives small typos. Use the sort chips at the top to order exercises by Default, Active Plan, Recent, or Frequent, so the exercises most relevant to you appear first. When replacing an exercise, the filter automatically preselects the matching target muscle to help you find alternatives faster. Tap any exercise to view its animated demonstration, the muscles targeted, and a full history of every time you have performed it, including weights, reps, time, or distance per set. Download all exercise animations (~100 MB) in Settings for offline access; the download needs an internet connection."
msgstr "Open the Exercise Library from the menu at any time to browse almost 1,000 exercises, and filter by body part, target muscle, or equipment. Search understands common abbreviations like RDL, OHP, DB, and KB, and forgives small typos. Use the sort chips at the top to order exercises by Default, Active Plan, Recent, or Frequent, so the exercises most relevant to you appear first. When replacing an exercise, the filter automatically preselects the matching target muscle to help you find alternatives faster. Tap any exercise to view its animated demonstration, the muscles targeted, and a full history of every time you have performed it, including weights, reps, time, or distance per set. Download all exercise animations (~100 MB) in Settings for offline access; the download needs an internet connection."

