#: constants/HelpData.ts:349
#~ msgid "Sign in with Google in Settings to enable cloud backups of all your workout data. Tap Backup at any time to save a snapshot; the date of your last backup is shown beneath the button. A backup that fails partway never replaces your last good one. Tap Restore to download and apply your latest backup. This replaces all training data on this device, so anything logged since that backup is lost; confirm the prompt and the app will reload with your restored data. Backup and restore need an internet connection. Your backups are stored securely and are tied to your Google account. If you switch devices or reinstall the app, simply sign in with the same Google account and tap Restore to get your data back."
#~ msgstr "Sign in with Google in Settings to enable cloud backups of all your workout data. Tap Backup at any time to save a snapshot; the date of your last backup is shown beneath the button. A backup that fails partway never replaces your last good one. Tap Restore to download and apply your latest backup. This replaces all training data on this device, so anything logged since that backup is lost; confirm the prompt and the app will reload with your restored data. Backup and restore need an internet connection. Your backups are stored securely and are tied to your Google account. If you switch devices or reinstall the app, simply sign in with the same Google account and tap Restore to get your data back."

#: constants/HelpData.ts:357
msgid "Sign in with Google in Settings to enable cloud backups of all your workout data. Tap Backup at any time to save a snapshot; the date of your last backup is shown beneath the button. A backup that fails partway never replaces your last good one. Tap Restore to download and apply your latest backup. This replaces all training data on this device, so anything logged since that backup is lost; confirm the prompt and the app will reload with your restored data. Backup and restore need an internet connection. Your backups are stored securely and are tied to your Google account. If you switch devices or reinstall the app, simply sign in with the same Google account and tap Restore to get your data back. The home screen reminds you when you have never backed up or your last backup is more than 30 days old."
msgstr "Sign in with Google in Settings to enable cloud backups of all your workout data. Tap Backup at any time to save a snapshot; the date of your last backup is shown beneath the button. A backup that fails partway never replaces your last good one. Tap Restore to download and apply your latest backup. This replaces all training data on this device, so anything logged since that backup is lost; confirm the prompt and the app will reload with your restored data. Backup and restore need an internet connection. Your backups are stored securely and are tied to your Google account. If you switch devices or reinstall the app, simply sign in with the same Google account and tap Restore to get your data back. The home screen reminds you when you have never backed up or your last backup is more than 30 days old."

