#: constants/HelpData.ts:38
#~ msgid "The home screen shows your progress toward your weekly training goal, which is the number of days you want to work out each week, set in Settings. A strip at the top tracks how many days you have completed and highlights each completed day; tap a highlighted day to view the workout you logged. Below it, your active plan's workouts are listed with their completion status for the week; tap Start on any workout to begin. If you are just starting out and have no active plan, a Pick a plan to get started card suggests a few premade plans instead. The card displayed beneath changes with your status: a Resume card appears if a session is in progress, a Rest Day card shows on days with no scheduled workout, and a Workout Done card confirms today's session is complete. When you hit your weekly goal, a Weekly Summary card appears showing total workouts, sets, and volume for the week, plus your streak, which counts the number of consecutive weeks you have met your goal. At the bottom, the Log Measurements card shows your latest body measurement; tap it to log today's values without leaving the screen."
#~ msgstr "The home screen shows your progress toward your weekly training goal, which is the number of days you want to work out each week, set in Settings. A strip at the top tracks how many days you have completed and highlights each completed day; tap a highlighted day to view the workout you logged. Below it, your active plan's workouts are listed with their completion status for the week; tap Start on any workout to begin. If you are just starting out and have no active plan, a Pick a plan to get started card suggests a few premade plans instead. The card displayed beneath changes with your status: a Resume card appears if a session is in progress, a Rest Day card shows on days with no scheduled workout, and a Workout Done card confirms today's session is complete. When you hit your weekly goal, a Weekly Summary card appears showing total workouts, sets, and volume for the week, plus your streak, which counts the number of consecutive weeks you have met your goal. At the bottom, the Log Measurements card shows your latest body measurement; tap it to log today's values without leaving the screen."

#: constants/HelpData.ts:38
msgid "The home screen shows your progress toward your weekly training goal, which is the number of days you want to work out each week, set in Settings. A strip at the top tracks how many days you have completed and highlights each completed day; tap a highlighted day to view the workout you logged. Below it, your active plan's workouts are listed with their completion status for the week; tap Start on any workout to begin. If you are just starting out and have no active plan, a Pick a plan to get started card suggests a few premade plans instead. The card displayed beneath changes with your status: a Resume card appears if a session is in progress, a Rest Day card shows on days with no scheduled workout, and a Workout Done card confirms today's session is complete. When you hit your weekly goal, a Weekly Summary card appears showing total workouts, sets, and volume for the week, plus your streak, which counts the number of consecutive weeks you have met your goal. At the bottom, the Log Measurements card shows your latest body measurement; tap it to log today's values without leaving the screen. If your training history has never been backed up, or your last backup is more than 30 days old, a reminder card appears here so you can back up or sign in on the spot; tap Later to hide it for two weeks."
msgstr "The home screen shows your progress toward your weekly training goal, which is the number of days you want to work out each week, set in Settings. A strip at the top tracks how many days you have completed and highlights each completed day; tap a highlighted day to view the workout you logged. Below it, your active plan's workouts are listed with their completion status for the week; tap Start on any workout to begin. If you are just starting out and have no active plan, a Pick a plan to get started card suggests a few premade plans instead. The card displayed beneath changes with your status: a Resume card appears if a session is in progress, a Rest Day card shows on days with no scheduled workout, and a Workout Done card confirms today's session is complete. When you hit your weekly goal, a Weekly Summary card appears showing total workouts, sets, and volume for the week, plus your streak, which counts the number of consecutive weeks you have met your goal. At the bottom, the Log Measurements card shows your latest body measurement; tap it to log today's values without leaving the screen. If your training history has never been backed up, or your last backup is more than 30 days old, a reminder card appears here so you can back up or sign in on the spot; tap Later to hide it for two weeks."

