#: constants/HelpData.ts:246
#~ msgid "The Stats tab shows total workouts, total volume, total time, and average session duration over a selectable time range, with a period-over-period delta for each metric. Charts display weekly volume and your training split by body part. Browse your full workout history and tap any session to review every set in detail, including weights, reps, time, or distance. You can edit or delete completed workouts from the history details screen. Tap the calendar icon in the Workout History section to open a calendar view: days with workouts are highlighted with a yellow circle, and tapping any day shows the workouts logged on that date."
#~ msgstr "The Stats tab shows total workouts, total volume, total time, and average session duration over a selectable time range, with a period-over-period delta for each metric. Charts display weekly volume and your training split by body part. Browse your full workout history and tap any session to review every set in detail, including weights, reps, time, or distance. You can edit or delete completed workouts from the history details screen. Tap the calendar icon in the Workout History section to open a calendar view: days with workouts are highlighted with a yellow circle, and tapping any day shows the workouts logged on that date."

#: constants/HelpData.ts:268
msgid "The Stats tab shows total workouts, total volume, total time, and average session duration over a selectable time range, with a period-over-period delta for each metric. Charts display weekly volume, workouts per week, and your training split by body part. Browse your full workout history and tap any session to review every set in detail, including weights, reps, time, or distance. You can edit or delete completed workouts from the history details screen; a deleted workout can be restored by tapping Undo on the message that appears. If you logged the wrong exercise, tap the pencil icon next to it on the edit screen to swap it for the correct one. Tap the calendar icon in the Workout History section to open a calendar view: days with workouts are highlighted with a yellow circle, and tapping any day shows the workouts logged on that date."
msgstr "The Stats tab shows total workouts, total volume, total time, and average session duration over a selectable time range, with a period-over-period delta for each metric. Charts display weekly volume, workouts per week, and your training split by body part. Browse your full workout history and tap any session to review every set in detail, including weights, reps, time, or distance. You can edit or delete completed workouts from the history details screen; a deleted workout can be restored by tapping Undo on the message that appears. If you logged the wrong exercise, tap the pencil icon next to it on the edit screen to swap it for the correct one. Tap the calendar icon in the Workout History section to open a calendar view: days with workouts are highlighted with a yellow circle, and tapping any day shows the workouts logged on that date."

